<title>CHINA: Mitsui and Co starts China steel venture.</title>
<headline>Mitsui and Co starts China steel venture.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A joint venture rolled steel processing plant by Japan's Mitsui and Co Ltd and Wuhan Iron and Steel Company of China has started operation in central Hubei province, the Xinhua news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company, with registered capital of 50 million yuan ($6 million), would use processing equipment imported from Japan and would focus on producing and processing cold-rolled silicon steel, the official agency said.</p>
<p>It gave no details of the expected output of the plant or breakdown of its ownership.</p>
</text>
